describe_photostim_groups(dat) — prints the group structure: for each real (power > 0) photostim group, its paired sham group (power = 0, same targeted cells), laser power, the targeted ROI indices, and the trial counts for real vs. sham. The pairing logic lives in photostim_group_map (photostim.py:9), which matches real/sham conditions by shared unique_group_id in markpoints.
plot_photostim_group_heatmaps(dat, mode='zscore') — one heatmap subplot per real group, side by side. Rows = cells (targeted cells sorted to the top and flagged with a purple dot at the row), columns = time (frames) around photostim onset (dashed line). Uses the coolwarm colormap. mode selects raw / per-cell peak-normalized / z-scored values. It excludes the all-NaN photostim-blanking frames from the normalization stats.
